title: One agent per slice
pid: 2b60a179-60a8-4099-982d-ad9d513e9ac7
body: |2-
  Launch one Opus agent per slice, at high effort, and wait for
  its report before launching the next. Its brief is the agent's
  only context; it does not see the discussion that produced the
  plan and should not need to. The brief holds:
  - the runner's prompt: the plan's path, the slice number, the
    progress file, the commit rule;
  - a "context carried forward" paragraph the orchestrator writes:
    what earlier slices built that this one relies on, names that
    changed since the plan was written, pitfalls found since;
  - the suites to run, each named with its command, with the
    instruction to serialize full runs (two at once collide on
    fixed temp paths and the Tantivy writer). List every suite
    whose assertions could depend on the slice's behavior, not
    only those whose code the slice touches: the AI tool's tests
    assert the server's behavior, and plan 4's briefs left them
    out, so one failed unseen for a day;
  - the tracked files that are dirty before the launch and whose
    they are, so that the agent neither commits Jeff's edits nor
    takes them for a stopped slice's leftovers;
  - where the record goes: the progress file's top-level headline
    for this plan, one subheadline per slice.
  Note the launch time before launching, for the cost record.
